sequenceDiagram
  %% route.destroy on the Gateway engine: the steps of route/destroy.mmd (workflow operation-route-removal) composed in the Gateway from host primitives (`file.read`, `config.apply`, `http.probe`). Built for ADR 0271 (RouteDestroyEngineFlow, Routes rewrite PR C).
  %% Every path, lock, owner, validator and unit arrives in the order; the Gateway renders each whole file. instance/container/destroy-engine.mmd still withdraws its Routes with `dns.publish_records` and `route.withdraw_site` until its own rewrite.
  %% status: built
  %% command: route:destroy
  %% kind: route.destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane EN icon=workflow pill=engine tone=purple
  %% lane N icon=server pill=executor tone=amber
  %% lane V icon=server pill=executor tone=green
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant EN as Engine<br/>Gateway and NATS
  participant N as Route Node<br/>executor
  participant V as VPN Node<br/>DNS executor
  CLI->>GW: route:destroy ROUTE
  Note over GW: Guard, capture placements<br/>Route unchanged
  %%> Same guards and captured states as route/destroy.mmd
  Note over GW: Hold the Route Nodes
  %%> Same hold as Swamp: each Node that serves the site, from admission to the terminal state; a second Route write on one of them waits
  alt the engine admits the whole Operation
    %%> Admission, one decision per Operation (EngineKinds::routes):
    %%> - `route.destroy` is in `ORBIT_ENGINE_KINDS`
    %%> - every Node a step touches reports its action in `$KV.NODES`: `file.read` and `config.apply` on each VPN Node, and `http.probe` too on each Route Node (agent 0.36.0)
    %%> - the flow accepts the plan shape; a part it does not cover throws `EngineUnsupported` before any order
    %%> - production gate (as ORB-6337): each serving Node has the active `app-dev` role and each DNS Node the `vpn` role; no `production_control`, and no production Instance on a serving Node
    %%> - eligible plan: an ordinary private Route with no URL write; `--offline`, Caddy access rows (`posix.acl.ensure` with scope `tree`, A4) or link writes, a never-activated replacement, LAN rules, an Ingress edge, `url_lines` for a surviving Route and any `env_files` write throw `EngineUnsupported`
    %%> - leaf folders and shared pools need the account's home and group, which only `account.read` (agent 0.37.0) reads on the Node; until that pin a removal with either runs on Swamp
    %%> - also refused: a public Route or a Process proxy (`route_private_development`), and a PHP version whose last shared pool would leave
    Note over GW: Bind steps, take the lock<br/>hold every Node, publish the start
    %%> - the step rows and the Operation lock commit in one transaction before the start event; an Operation never moves between engines after this
    %%> - in the same transaction the start refuses `route.publication_held` while another open Route write, on either engine, writes or holds one of its Nodes, the DNS-only VPN Nodes included (RouteWriteNodes); an engine removal fences later Route writes the same way
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
    opt domain outside the TLD
      EN->>V: Read records and catalog<br/>file.read · dnsread-i
      %%> Two reads, never following a link: the digest, type, owner and mode of `/etc/dnsmasq.d/orbit-records.conf` and `/var/lib/orbit/private-dns/catalog.json`; the receipt is the step's output, so a retry sends the same guard
      %%> Anything but a plain file or nothing refuses (`owned_revision_conflict`)
      V-->>EN: Digest or absent
      EN->>V: Write records and catalog<br/>config.apply · dns-i
      %%> The records and catalog rendered without the Route, each guarded by the digest just read (`from_sha256`; none for an absent file), owner `root:root 0644`, under the DNS lock `/run/lock/orbit-dnsmasq.lock`
      %%> A file that changed since the read refuses before any write (`owned_revision_conflict`); bytes that differ only in form (another key order) are rewritten to the Gateway's render
      %%> `dnsmasq --test` with `/etc/dnsmasq.conf` and `/etc/dnsmasq.d`, then `dnsmasq` and `orbit-private-dns` restart on every run; a failed test or restart puts the old files back and loads them again
      %%> The prior state is recorded in `/var/lib/orbit/executor/recovery/operation-<id>/dns-<i>`, so a run that stopped is undone by its replay
      V-->>EN: Files and restart<br/>applied
      Note over EN: Wait the DNS grace<br/>31 s: TTL 30 s + 1 s
      %%> A Gateway step (`grace`) after every `dns-i`: it runs no earlier than 31 s after the last recorded DNS receipt (`done_ms`), as Swamp's `route-dns-grace`; a redelivered receipt or a resend never moves that time
      %%> The engine keeps that time on the step (`EngineWait`) and schedules its deadline on the bus; no process sleeps, so a restart resumes only what is left (ORB-6333)
      %%> A cancel during the wait ends the Operation `cancelled` with nothing withdrawn from the Route Node
    end
    EN->>N: Read the Caddyfile<br/>file.read · caddyread-node
    N-->>EN: Digest
    Note over EN: Guard the Caddyfile<br/>guard-node
    %%> A Gateway step: the read digest must be the Caddyfile rendered at admission (`route_guards`) or the desired one, else `owned_revision_conflict` and nothing is written; a link in its place refuses too
    EN->>N: Write and reload Caddy<br/>config.apply · withdraw-node
    %%> The whole Caddyfile without the Route, guarded by the digest read, owner `root:caddy 0640`, under the publication lock `/etc/caddy/.orbit-publish.lock`
    %%> `caddy validate` as `caddy`, then `caddy.service` reloads on every run, also a replay that finds nothing to change; a failed validation or reload puts the old file back and reloads it
    %%> Recovery record in `/var/lib/orbit/executor/recovery/operation-<id>/withdraw-<node>`
    N-->>EN: applied
    EN->>N: Poll Caddy's admin API<br/>http.probe · poll-node
    %%> `http://127.0.0.1:2019/config/` until no withdrawn name appears in it, within 5 s (ORB-6335); unmet fails the chart's withdrawal step
    N-->>EN: met
    EN->>N: Probe a sibling Route<br/>TLS over WireGuard
    %%> A Gateway step (`sibling-node`) as route.create's probe: a TLS handshake with another Route on the same Node, trusting only the Orbit root, proves Caddy still serves the rest; skipped when the Node serves no other Route
    opt the receipt is lost
      EN->>N: Resend the same step<br/>fresh nonce · same step ID
      %%> When:
      %%> - the step passes its resend deadline with no receipt; two sends, one execution
      %%> - the Operation keeps its lock, so the Route and its held Nodes stays fenced; no other Operation and no Swamp run acts on it meanwhile
      %%> On the Node:
      %%> - the journal holds `done` for this Operation step, action and target: the executor answers the stored result with `repeat: true` and does not act again
      %%> - an order still `open` replays under the target lock first; an order that expired before the lock did nothing (`executor.order_expired`), and the step is sent again
      N-->>EN: Stored result<br/>repeat: true
    end
    alt every step verified
      EN->>GW: Delete the Route record<br/>free the held Nodes
      %%> - the kind's own projection records the result, the same rows a Swamp run records: the Route goes `retiring` before its record is deleted, and the only authoritative Route of an active Instance stays (ORB-6339); a projection that throws is retried twice, then fails `engine.projection_failed`
    else a step fails
      EN--xGW: Failed step<br/>error_code · redacted detail
      %%> - a deterministic refusal is a terminal receipt too; the journal keeps it and a resend repeats it
      Note over GW: Record the failure<br/>Route kept · failed step
      %%> - what was withdrawn stays withdrawn; no rollback
      %%> - each step maps onto the Swamp chart step it is part of (reads, guard and poll onto `Withdraw site, remove cert` or `Remove private DNS`), so the projection records main's `failed_step` and that step's code
      %%> - retry: the same command; its reads take the files as they are and each write converges
    end
  else the engine does not admit it
    Note over GW: Start the Swamp run<br/>operation-route-removal
    %%> - the kind is not enabled, a Node lacks the action, `$KV.NODES` is unreadable, or the flow throws `EngineUnsupported`: the whole Operation runs operation-route-removal (route/destroy.mmd)
    %%> - no step of it runs on the engine; an Operation never splits across engines
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
